course: dictionary
lesson: 15274
title: Formal words: signify
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Signify is a formal word that means to be a sign of something, or to mean something. When you see signify, ask: what is this a sign of? «Dark clouds signify rain.» Dark clouds are a sign that rain is coming, so signify means to be a sign of.
explain: Signify can also mean to show a feeling or wish, often by an action. «She nodded to signify yes.» She did not say the word. Her nod showed she agreed, so the nod was the sign.
explain: Signify is often used in maths and science. «The plus sign signifies addition.» The + symbol tells you to add. Signs and symbols are always telling you something, so look for what they stand for.
fact: Signify is a verb. Its forms are signify, signifies, signified and signifying.
fact: «Signify» means to be a sign of something, or to mean something.
fact: «Signify» can also mean to show a feeling or wish by a sign or action, like a nod.
fact: «It does not signify» means it is not important, so it does not matter.
fact: In maths, symbols signify operations: + signifies addition.
exercise: «Dark clouds signify rain.» What does signify mean here? | To fall quickly from the sky | To make a loud noise | *To be a sign of something | To be very dark and cold
exercise: «She nodded to signify yes.» What did her nod do? | It was a sneeze | *It showed she agreed | It made the room darker | It meant she was tired
exercise: In maths, the + sign signifies what? | Multiplication | Division | Subtraction | *Addition
test: Lily says, «It does not signify if we are late.» What does this mean? | *It does not matter | It is a secret | It is a sign of danger | Being late is very important
test: «A red light on the road signifies stop.» What does the red light show? | That the bus is late | That the road is closed for lunch | That it is raining | *That drivers must stop
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to signify in «A raised hand can signify a vote»? | hurt | sleep | hide | *mean
